---
.title = "Frame messages on a TCP stream",
.date = "2024-01-01",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

TCP preserves byte order, but it does not preserve application message boundaries. A receiver
may get one write in several reads, or several writes in one read. This example prefixes a
payload with its four-byte length, then reads exactly one complete frame. It uses an in-memory
stream to keep the framing logic deterministic; the same framing works on a TCP connection.

